1
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:43,680
Mom, where are you now?

2
00:01:45,200 --> 00:01:47,040
Just past Innovation Industrial Park.

3
00:01:49,160 --> 00:01:50,520
You didn't reply to my text.

4
00:01:50,600 --> 00:01:52,800
I called just in case
you missed your stop.

5
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:55,360
I don't go out often,

6
00:01:55,440 --> 00:01:58,040
but I know how to read bus stop signs.

7
00:01:58,120 --> 00:01:59,240
<i>What if you dozed off?</i>

8
00:02:01,720 --> 00:02:03,560
That is possible.

9
00:02:05,440 --> 00:02:08,759
I used to always look down, volunteering
and picking up trash with everyone.

10
00:02:09,680 --> 00:02:12,720
<i>Now I've realized that our city</i>
<i>is very beautiful.</i>

11
00:02:12,800 --> 00:02:14,280
<i>It's so scenic.</i>

12
00:02:15,400 --> 00:02:17,440
If you like it, I'll tell Dad.

13
00:02:17,520 --> 00:02:18,800
In the future,

14
00:02:19,640 --> 00:02:20,880
we can go out more often.

15
00:02:21,480 --> 00:02:22,400
Sure.

16
00:02:22,960 --> 00:02:24,760
Let's all go out together.

17
00:02:26,600 --> 00:02:28,320
<i>By the way, have you eaten yet?</i>

18
00:02:28,400 --> 00:02:29,920
Doing experiments is tiring,

19
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:31,880
but don't forget to eat.

20
00:02:33,840 --> 00:02:34,680
Hello?

21
00:02:35,800 --> 00:02:36,920
Hello?

22
00:02:54,120 --> 00:02:58,000
<i>You're busy studying and writing a thesis.</i>

23
00:02:58,080 --> 00:02:59,560
<i>I already called a cab.</i>

24
00:02:59,640 --> 00:03:00,880
<i>It will be here soon.</i>

25
00:03:00,960 --> 00:03:02,000
<i>Yanzhou.</i>

26
00:03:02,080 --> 00:03:03,400
<i>I'll go with you.</i>

27
00:03:14,240 --> 00:03:15,200
Where to?

28
00:03:16,760 --> 00:03:18,280
Innovation Industrial Park.

29
00:03:19,680 --> 00:03:20,920
No, wait.

30
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:23,640
Go to the hospital.
The closest one to that park.

31
00:03:24,440 --> 00:03:25,400
Okay.

32
00:03:43,040 --> 00:03:44,520
Sir, how much longer?

33
00:03:45,280 --> 00:03:48,520
It's all red on the GPS.
Drivers are saying there was an accident.

34
00:03:49,160 --> 00:03:51,240
I really don't know how long it will take.

35
00:03:51,320 --> 00:03:52,440
An accident?

36
00:03:53,080 --> 00:03:56,040
- How far are we from the hospital?
- Close to 3 km.

37
00:04:00,920 --> 00:04:02,600
Sir, I've already paid the fare.

38
00:04:02,680 --> 00:04:03,520
Okay, thank you.

39
00:04:05,920 --> 00:04:08,280
Dad, I've asked. It's this hospital.

40
00:04:18,760 --> 00:04:21,399
What exactly did Yanzhou say on the phone?

41
00:04:21,480 --> 00:04:23,520
He doesn't know the details either.

42
00:04:23,600 --> 00:04:25,960
Something happened
to the bus that Ailan was on.

43
00:04:26,040 --> 00:04:28,160
I called Ailan but couldn't get through.

44
00:04:28,240 --> 00:04:31,000
I called the bus company,
but the line was busy.

45
00:04:31,080 --> 00:04:33,400
Mom, Huaguang, don't panic.

46
00:04:33,480 --> 00:04:35,920
No news might actually be good news.

47
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:38,560
Isn't that Yanzhou?

48
00:04:41,760 --> 00:04:43,680
- What happened?
- Grandma.

49
00:04:43,760 --> 00:04:45,000
Why did you run here?

50
00:04:45,080 --> 00:04:47,160
Don't you know that you shouldn't run?

51
00:04:47,240 --> 00:04:49,720
Mom, let's not
talk about that. Let's go inside.

52
00:04:49,800 --> 00:04:51,360
- Let's go.
- Let's go inside.

53
00:04:55,640 --> 00:04:58,960
Nurse, were there any patients
brought in from a bus accident?

54
00:04:59,040 --> 00:05:00,160
Over there.

55
00:05:01,800 --> 00:05:03,080
Thank you.

56
00:05:03,160 --> 00:05:04,360
You're welcome.

57
00:05:05,920 --> 00:05:07,880
The photos and videos are still here.

58
00:05:07,960 --> 00:05:08,800
That's great.

59
00:05:09,680 --> 00:05:12,760
Thank you. You've been working
on this all afternoon.

60
00:05:12,840 --> 00:05:14,360
Of course, no problem.

61
00:05:14,440 --> 00:05:16,600
Yes, it should be over there.

62
00:05:17,920 --> 00:05:20,120
- It looks like she's fine.
- Yanzhou?

63
00:05:20,840 --> 00:05:21,680
Why are you here?

64
00:05:23,480 --> 00:05:24,680
You all…

65
00:05:24,760 --> 00:05:26,560
Why are you all here?

66
00:05:26,640 --> 00:05:27,600
Are you okay?

67
00:05:27,680 --> 00:05:28,960
How are you?

68
00:05:29,040 --> 00:05:30,080
I'm fine.

69
00:05:32,200 --> 00:05:33,400
Chen Yanzhou.

70
00:05:35,400 --> 00:05:36,960
Why are you here?

71
00:05:37,040 --> 00:05:38,800
She was on the same bus as me.

72
00:05:38,880 --> 00:05:40,240
She went to pay my bill.

73
00:05:40,320 --> 00:05:41,680
I'm glad she was here.

74
00:05:41,760 --> 00:05:43,480
Thank you.

75
00:05:43,560 --> 00:05:44,960
Are you sure you're okay?

76
00:05:45,040 --> 00:05:47,960
I really am okay.
The bus crashed into a stone bollard.

77
00:05:48,040 --> 00:05:49,440
The driver braked hard.

78
00:05:49,520 --> 00:05:52,040
I have a strained back
and superficial injuries.

79
00:05:52,120 --> 00:05:53,160
It's nothing serious.

80
00:05:53,240 --> 00:05:54,360
You look so worried.

81
00:05:54,440 --> 00:05:55,280
She looks okay.

82
00:05:55,880 --> 00:05:57,480
Luckily, it was a minor accident.

83
00:05:58,080 --> 00:06:00,880
Aunt, we were taking Grandma out to eat.

84
00:06:00,960 --> 00:06:01,880
We had just left.

85
00:06:01,960 --> 00:06:04,640
When we heard the news,
we were so worried.

86
00:06:04,720 --> 00:06:07,720
You're exaggerating.
It's good that your aunt is fine.

87
00:06:07,800 --> 00:06:09,200
Why didn't you pick up?

88
00:06:14,600 --> 00:06:17,520
Did you forget
that we were talking on the phone?

89
00:06:20,200 --> 00:06:21,200
All afternoon.

90
00:06:22,480 --> 00:06:24,840
Didn't it occur to you
to tell me you were safe?

91
00:06:25,880 --> 00:06:28,400
I had dropped my phone,
and the screen went black.

92
00:06:28,480 --> 00:06:30,440
It wouldn't turn on.

93
00:06:31,240 --> 00:06:33,720
I borrowed the nurse's phone
to see how to fix it.

94
00:06:33,800 --> 00:06:36,840
I fixed it just before you all arrived.

95
00:06:37,560 --> 00:06:41,160
Fortunately,
everything on the phone is intact.

96
00:06:41,240 --> 00:06:42,120
It's a miracle.

97
00:06:42,800 --> 00:06:43,840
Do you know

98
00:06:43,920 --> 00:06:46,440
how hard Yanzhou ran to find you?

99
00:06:47,040 --> 00:06:49,000
In the end, it's just a lousy phone.

100
00:06:49,080 --> 00:06:50,320
- Give it to me.
- What?

101
00:06:50,400 --> 00:06:51,600
- Give me the phone!
- Mom.

102
00:06:51,680 --> 00:06:54,520
- Give me the phone!
- Don't take it! Don't take my phone!

103
00:06:56,200 --> 00:06:58,280
<i>Ms. Zhou, long time no see.</i>

104
00:06:58,360 --> 00:07:00,560
<i>To attend this international summer camp,</i>

105
00:07:00,640 --> 00:07:02,640
<i>I couldn't go home for New Year's.</i>

106
00:07:02,720 --> 00:07:04,680
<i>If I had known, I wouldn't have come.</i>

107
00:07:05,480 --> 00:07:07,800
<i>Ms. Zhou, in this new year,</i>

108
00:07:07,880 --> 00:07:09,240
<i>may you continue to succeed</i>

109
00:07:09,320 --> 00:07:12,040
<i>and become</i>
<i>the best environmental engineer.</i>

110
00:07:13,080 --> 00:07:14,800
<i>You're allowed to ditch us sometimes</i>

111
00:07:14,880 --> 00:07:16,160
<i>as long as you remember</i>

112
00:07:16,240 --> 00:07:18,400
<i>that we are always here for you.</i>

113
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:21,920
Mom, doesn't she have amnesia?

114
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:23,840
Does she remember?

115
00:07:23,920 --> 00:07:24,760
<i>By the way,</i>

116
00:07:25,360 --> 00:07:28,440
<i>I also filmed clips for Dad and Yanzhou.</i>

117
00:07:28,520 --> 00:07:29,880
<i>Yours is the longest.</i>

118
00:07:40,840 --> 00:07:41,920
What does this mean?

119
00:07:43,200 --> 00:07:44,640
Today, did the crash

120
00:07:45,680 --> 00:07:47,800
knock you back to your senses?

121
00:07:48,560 --> 00:07:51,800
Or have you been lying to us
all these years?

122
00:07:54,400 --> 00:07:55,800
What right do you have…

123
00:07:58,040 --> 00:07:58,960
to touch my phone?

124
00:07:59,040 --> 00:08:01,120
If I hadn't, I wouldn't have known!

125
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:06,160
Every day, you appear to remember nothing.

126
00:08:07,040 --> 00:08:09,800
But it turns out you had us all fooled!

127
00:08:11,400 --> 00:08:12,680
If Xiaoqi

128
00:08:12,760 --> 00:08:15,600
knew that his mother was like this now…

129
00:08:15,680 --> 00:08:16,600
Mom,

130
00:08:17,240 --> 00:08:19,560
Ailan is injured right now.

131
00:08:19,640 --> 00:08:22,840
She's injured, so everything
has to revolve around her?!

132
00:08:22,920 --> 00:08:25,960
These past years,
haven't we played along long enough?

133
00:08:26,040 --> 00:08:28,160
Mom, this is a hospital.

134
00:08:28,240 --> 00:08:29,480
Let's not say all this.

135
00:08:29,560 --> 00:08:30,600
Not say all this?!

136
00:08:30,680 --> 00:08:32,400
I've barely begun to say anything!

137
00:08:32,480 --> 00:08:34,240
I was wrong, all right?

138
00:08:34,320 --> 00:08:36,120
Why did you have to take my phone?

139
00:08:36,200 --> 00:08:38,200
Would I have known otherwise?

140
00:08:38,280 --> 00:08:40,480
But you shouldn't have touched my phone!

141
00:08:40,559 --> 00:08:42,320
Why did you touch my phone?

142
00:08:42,400 --> 00:08:44,400
- Why can't I?
- Why did you turn it on?

143
00:08:44,480 --> 00:08:46,280
What right do you have to touch it?

144
00:08:46,360 --> 00:08:47,200
Why can't I?

145
00:08:47,280 --> 00:08:50,280
I had to take your phone,
or I wouldn't have known!

146
00:08:50,360 --> 00:08:52,000
Ma'am, your phone is fine. Look.

147
00:08:52,080 --> 00:08:54,400
Anger will make you sick.

148
00:08:55,080 --> 00:08:56,160
All right now.

149
00:08:56,240 --> 00:08:57,440
Look, it's fine.

150
00:08:57,520 --> 00:08:59,200
Your files are still here.

151
00:09:03,200 --> 00:09:06,280
I'll leave these reports with you.

152
00:09:06,360 --> 00:09:08,360
Your exam report looks fine.

153
00:09:08,440 --> 00:09:09,720
Get some rest. Bye now.

154
00:09:12,960 --> 00:09:16,280
How do you know
my phone's passcode is 990508?

155
00:09:16,360 --> 00:09:19,840
I helped to fix your phone
during Lunar New Year.

156
00:09:19,920 --> 00:09:22,080
Chen Yanzhou told me the passcode.

157
00:09:31,120 --> 00:09:32,440
990508.

158
00:09:35,760 --> 00:09:37,960
It's the day that Guanqi was born.

159
00:09:43,120 --> 00:09:47,920
So Yanzhou knew long ago.

160
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:07,480
Don't lie there anymore.

161
00:10:08,440 --> 00:10:10,080
At least get up and eat a bit.

162
00:10:10,680 --> 00:10:12,320
I don't want to eat.

163
00:10:12,400 --> 00:10:14,040
Think about Yanzhou.

164
00:10:14,120 --> 00:10:16,240
He didn't speak much to begin with.

165
00:10:16,320 --> 00:10:18,240
Now he barely says a word.

166
00:10:18,320 --> 00:10:20,000
Come, get up.

167
00:10:20,080 --> 00:10:21,400
Go and talk to him.

168
00:10:21,480 --> 00:10:23,320
Sorry, I can't.

169
00:10:23,400 --> 00:10:25,080
Yanzhou is fortunate.

170
00:10:25,160 --> 00:10:27,080
He wasn't hurt much.

171
00:10:27,160 --> 00:10:29,040
But when I see him,

172
00:10:29,120 --> 00:10:31,480
I'm reminded of Guanqi.

173
00:10:31,560 --> 00:10:33,840
Guanqi was completely…

174
00:10:35,120 --> 00:10:36,840
I'm sorry, I can't help it.

175
00:10:37,920 --> 00:10:40,760
<i>I can't help but think about him.</i>

176
00:10:41,640 --> 00:10:43,080
<i>Hello, Dad.</i>

177
00:10:43,160 --> 00:10:45,520
I'm done with the exam.
I'm on my way home.

178
00:10:45,600 --> 00:10:48,560
<i>Yanzhou, don't go home yet.</i>
<i>Come to the hospital.</i>

179
00:10:48,640 --> 00:10:50,760
<i>Your mom fell down the stairs.</i>

180
00:10:50,840 --> 00:10:52,560
<i>She's in the hospital now.</i>

181
00:10:53,440 --> 00:10:55,400
Why did she fall?

182
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:57,600
<i>Don't ask so many questions.</i>

183
00:10:57,680 --> 00:10:59,040
<i>Be prepared.</i>

184
00:10:59,120 --> 00:10:59,960
<i>Your mom…</i>

185
00:11:01,240 --> 00:11:02,920
<i>Your mom lost her memories.</i>

186
00:11:07,640 --> 00:11:08,960
PROPERTY MANAGEMENT

187
00:11:15,600 --> 00:11:17,240
- Hello.
- <i>Hello, Ms. Zhou.</i>

188
00:11:17,320 --> 00:11:19,000
<i>This is your property management.</i>

189
00:11:19,080 --> 00:11:20,960
<i>May I have two minutes of your time?</i>

190
00:11:22,120 --> 00:11:23,360
What is it?

191
00:11:23,440 --> 00:11:25,640
<i>To further enhance</i>
<i>our community's security</i>

192
00:11:25,720 --> 00:11:27,080
<i>and ease of entry and exit,</i>

193
00:11:27,160 --> 00:11:30,760
<i>we will be upgrading</i>
<i>the main gate security system this week</i>

194
00:11:30,840 --> 00:11:32,520
<i>and adding facial recognition.</i>

195
00:11:32,600 --> 00:11:35,280
<i>Detailed instructions on how to use it</i>

196
00:11:35,360 --> 00:11:37,240
<i>have been sent to you via text.</i>

197
00:11:37,320 --> 00:11:40,080
<i>We ask that you and your family</i>
<i>register on our app</i>

198
00:11:40,160 --> 00:11:41,600
<i>as soon as possible.</i>

199
00:11:41,680 --> 00:11:43,160
Okay, thank you.

200
00:11:45,680 --> 00:11:48,160
MS. ZHOU, TO COORDINATE
WITH THE COMMUNITY'S GATE…

201
00:11:48,240 --> 00:11:49,480
ENTER PASSCODE

202
00:11:52,240 --> 00:11:53,400
Mom.

203
00:12:17,560 --> 00:12:18,720
Your mom is sleeping.

204
00:12:19,880 --> 00:12:20,800
What is it?

205
00:12:21,880 --> 00:12:22,880
Nothing.

206
00:12:25,520 --> 00:12:26,560
Dad.

207
00:12:28,040 --> 00:12:30,200
When you bought the phone for Mom,

208
00:12:30,280 --> 00:12:31,800
did you set the passcode?

209
00:12:31,880 --> 00:12:33,000
No.

210
00:12:33,080 --> 00:12:34,840
That's considered personal privacy.

211
00:12:34,920 --> 00:12:36,680
It's better if I don't know.

212
00:13:06,880 --> 00:13:08,600
Fatso, let's just go get the key.

213
00:13:08,680 --> 00:13:10,120
Who do we ask for the key?

214
00:13:10,200 --> 00:13:11,400
Mr. Li, right?

215
00:13:11,480 --> 00:13:14,360
Mr. Li won't be on campus anymore
at this hour.

216
00:13:14,440 --> 00:13:15,440
Let's ask security.

217
00:13:15,520 --> 00:13:17,240
They should have the key.

218
00:13:17,320 --> 00:13:18,520
What happened?

219
00:13:31,560 --> 00:13:33,080
<i>Not at home, not at the lab.</i>

220
00:13:33,160 --> 00:13:34,720
<i>He doesn't live on campus.</i>

221
00:13:34,800 --> 00:13:35,800
<i>Where can he go?</i>

222
00:13:35,880 --> 00:13:39,560
Hello, Mr. Li.
Did Chen Yanzhou contact you today?

223
00:13:39,640 --> 00:13:41,320
<i>No, he didn't.</i>

224
00:13:41,400 --> 00:13:44,320
<i>His paper was rejected.</i>

225
00:13:47,240 --> 00:13:48,760
<i>The old lab.</i>

226
00:13:56,840 --> 00:13:59,400
Wasn't that lab next door abandoned?

227
00:13:59,480 --> 00:14:01,360
Who knew there was thale cress inside?

228
00:14:01,440 --> 00:14:03,200
- And so many.
- How tragic.

229
00:14:03,280 --> 00:14:05,440
Those had to be for experiments.

230
00:14:05,520 --> 00:14:07,000
- They're all ruined now.
- Yes.

231
00:14:07,080 --> 00:14:08,120
Wait.

232
00:14:09,600 --> 00:14:11,240
What did you say is ruined?

233
00:14:12,080 --> 00:14:14,800
Lab 305 in the old building
was disinfected today.

234
00:14:14,880 --> 00:14:17,960
The people in the lab thought
the lab next door was abandoned

235
00:14:18,040 --> 00:14:18,920
and didn't notice.

236
00:14:19,000 --> 00:14:21,760
<i>The disinfectant vapors</i>
<i>traveled next door through the vent.</i>

237
00:14:21,840 --> 00:14:24,480
<i>Thale cress was being grown</i>
<i>in the abandoned lab.</i>

238
00:14:24,560 --> 00:14:26,360
<i>After a day, they're all dead now.</i>

239
00:15:11,480 --> 00:15:15,120
I was going to change the water
for the thale cress at noon.

240
00:15:15,920 --> 00:15:16,840
But

241
00:15:17,680 --> 00:15:19,880
I couldn't reach my mom on the phone.

242
00:15:20,760 --> 00:15:22,640
And now, I come back to…

243
00:15:44,360 --> 00:15:47,200
<i>When the immune system operates,</i>

244
00:15:47,280 --> 00:15:50,600
<i>it must distinguish</i>
<i>between self and non-self.</i>

245
00:15:52,120 --> 00:15:55,160
<i>Sometimes, this complex system will crash,</i>

246
00:15:55,240 --> 00:15:57,360
<i>causing the system to mistake the self</i>

247
00:15:57,440 --> 00:15:59,600
<i>for a foreign body</i>
<i>that needs to be removed.</i>

248
00:16:00,400 --> 00:16:02,040
<i>This person in front of me</i>

249
00:16:03,040 --> 00:16:06,240
<i>seems to have identified himself</i>
<i>as a foreign body to be removed.</i>

250
00:16:07,520 --> 00:16:09,320
<i>It's so heartbreaking,</i>

251
00:16:09,840 --> 00:16:11,680
<i>to the point that my misfortune,</i>

252
00:16:11,760 --> 00:16:13,520
<i>my pride,</i>

253
00:16:13,600 --> 00:16:15,880
<i>and everything else that wears me down</i>

254
00:16:17,120 --> 00:16:19,360
<i>seems insignificant at this moment.</i>

255
00:16:20,640 --> 00:16:21,960
<i>All I know is</i>

256
00:16:22,720 --> 00:16:24,520
<i>that I cannot abandon</i>

257
00:16:25,440 --> 00:16:27,240
<i>this person in front of me.</i>

258
00:16:30,640 --> 00:16:31,880
When you left,

259
00:16:31,960 --> 00:16:33,520
was my mom okay?

260
00:16:36,720 --> 00:16:39,200
I shouldn't have said those words.

261
00:16:39,280 --> 00:16:40,920
She was injured.

262
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:42,600
I shouldn't have blamed her.

263
00:16:42,680 --> 00:16:43,640
You can blame her.

264
00:16:48,600 --> 00:16:50,400
What I mean is,

265
00:16:50,480 --> 00:16:52,880
you don't have
to blame yourself for everything.

266
00:16:53,560 --> 00:16:58,120
Before I came here, I learned that
your mom's phone passcode

267
00:16:58,200 --> 00:16:59,960
is your brother's birthdate.

268
00:17:01,080 --> 00:17:04,599
You knew long ago
that she remembered everything.

269
00:17:10,040 --> 00:17:11,920
Why didn't you say anything?

270
00:17:15,079 --> 00:17:16,880
I was afraid she couldn't take it,

271
00:17:17,480 --> 00:17:21,960
just like how she fell down the stairs
after my brother passed away.

272
00:17:23,040 --> 00:17:25,800
I was afraid I couldn't take it either.

273
00:17:25,880 --> 00:17:27,440
I was afraid

274
00:17:27,520 --> 00:17:31,240
of causing an irreversible situation
like six years ago.

275
00:17:33,960 --> 00:17:36,880
I thought that if I worked hard
to follow in my brother's footsteps,

276
00:17:38,360 --> 00:17:41,680
even if I made a mistake
that can't be undone,

277
00:17:41,760 --> 00:17:43,240
at least

278
00:17:44,400 --> 00:17:46,320
I could bring comfort to everyone.

279
00:17:50,400 --> 00:17:52,440
You don't need to learn calligraphy.

280
00:17:52,520 --> 00:17:54,680
You don't need
to eat foods you don't like.

281
00:17:56,040 --> 00:17:59,080
Nor do you need
to replace "Mom" with "Ms. Zhou."

282
00:17:59,160 --> 00:18:01,640
You can be yourself.

283
00:18:01,720 --> 00:18:03,520
You don't need to comfort anyone.

284
00:18:04,760 --> 00:18:07,840
Because surviving that accident

285
00:18:07,920 --> 00:18:09,600
is a comfort in itself.

286
00:18:39,240 --> 00:18:40,360
Yanzhou.

287
00:20:26,360 --> 00:20:29,440
CHLORPHENIRAMINE MALEATE

288
00:20:36,200 --> 00:20:39,120
NOTOGINSENG MIND CALMING TABLETS

289
00:20:46,520 --> 00:20:48,680
FOR USE IN ALLEVIATING SYMPTOMS
OF ALLERGIC REACTIONS

290
00:20:50,560 --> 00:20:51,800
<i>I learned only recently</i>

291
00:20:52,400 --> 00:20:55,440
<i>that some people are allergic to eggs.</i>

292
00:20:55,520 --> 00:20:58,000
Are there people who are allergic to eggs?

293
00:20:58,080 --> 00:21:01,240
Especially people
who have been seriously ill.

294
00:21:02,040 --> 00:21:03,800
<i>They may seem to have recovered,</i>

295
00:21:03,880 --> 00:21:06,160
<i>but their bodies have weakened immunity</i>

296
00:21:06,240 --> 00:21:08,120
<i>and develop new allergies.</i>

297
00:21:12,160 --> 00:21:14,560
FLUPENTIXOL AND MELITRACEN TABLETS

298
00:21:16,800 --> 00:21:17,720
<i>Mom.</i>

299
00:21:18,920 --> 00:21:21,480
I don't like scrambled eggs
with tomatoes now.

300
00:21:22,240 --> 00:21:24,320
Didn't you still like it not long ago?

301
00:21:26,000 --> 00:21:28,320
People's preferences can change.

302
00:21:28,400 --> 00:21:31,360
I can share my preferences, right?

303
00:22:39,600 --> 00:22:40,720
Mom.

304
00:22:45,840 --> 00:22:47,800
- Sor--
- Sorry.

305
00:23:14,760 --> 00:23:16,040
Sorry.

306
00:23:22,000 --> 00:23:23,240
I'm sorry.

307
00:23:34,760 --> 00:23:36,120
I'm sorry.

308
00:23:40,200 --> 00:23:41,520
It's my fault.

309
00:23:46,640 --> 00:23:48,280
I'm sorry.

310
00:23:53,960 --> 00:23:55,440
Sorry.

311
00:24:02,000 --> 00:24:03,440
I feel that

312
00:24:04,920 --> 00:24:07,040
I am such a failure as a mother.

313
00:24:12,080 --> 00:24:14,240
After losing your brother…

314
00:24:16,480 --> 00:24:18,360
I asked myself these questions every day.

315
00:24:18,960 --> 00:24:21,400
If I'd been the one
who'd gone with you that day…

316
00:24:23,360 --> 00:24:26,800
would I have been the one
who died instead?

317
00:24:29,480 --> 00:24:31,680
If I'd been driving that day,

318
00:24:31,760 --> 00:24:33,760
would I have taken a different route?

319
00:24:34,760 --> 00:24:37,320
If I had called him
to warn him more than I did,

320
00:24:37,400 --> 00:24:39,880
would the outcome have been different?

321
00:24:43,800 --> 00:24:45,320
You and your dad

322
00:24:46,800 --> 00:24:48,400
must have been the same as me.

323
00:24:50,200 --> 00:24:54,520
Your minds must also have been filled
with these hypothetical what-ifs.

324
00:24:57,040 --> 00:24:58,280
I know

325
00:24:59,200 --> 00:25:01,440
it was really hard to accept.

326
00:25:04,880 --> 00:25:06,040
Later on,

327
00:25:06,120 --> 00:25:09,600
I accidentally fell down the stairs.

328
00:25:11,120 --> 00:25:13,400
When I woke up, I had lost my memory.

329
00:25:17,040 --> 00:25:20,200
You and your dad played along with me…

330
00:25:22,600 --> 00:25:24,760
never talking about Guanqi.

331
00:25:28,560 --> 00:25:29,840
But…

332
00:25:33,000 --> 00:25:34,840
But soon after, I remembered it all.

333
00:25:39,360 --> 00:25:41,640
On the day that my memory returned,

334
00:25:42,600 --> 00:25:43,600
I rushed downstairs.

335
00:26:01,920 --> 00:26:03,520
<i>I saw you and your dad</i>

336
00:26:03,600 --> 00:26:05,440
<i>waving me over with smiles.</i>

337
00:26:08,960 --> 00:26:12,520
<i>I wondered if continuing like this</i>
<i>would be best for everyone.</i>

338
00:26:16,040 --> 00:26:20,120
<i>If I didn't show my pain…</i>

339
00:26:22,360 --> 00:26:24,360
<i>would it not hurt as much?</i>

340
00:26:28,720 --> 00:26:30,200
I am such a fool.

341
00:26:32,880 --> 00:26:35,960
I didn't even consider what my kind child

342
00:26:37,120 --> 00:26:39,200
was enduring.

343
00:26:40,880 --> 00:26:43,480
Look how you have worn yourself out.

344
00:26:43,560 --> 00:26:45,600
Why didn't I ever notice?

345
00:26:47,680 --> 00:26:48,880
Or perhaps…

346
00:26:51,000 --> 00:26:52,760
I chose to turn a blind eye.

347
00:26:59,760 --> 00:27:01,080
I'm sorry.

348
00:27:05,560 --> 00:27:08,080
I lost one child.

349
00:27:10,200 --> 00:27:12,520
And yet, I'm hurting my other child.

350
00:27:16,040 --> 00:27:17,480
Sorry.

351
00:27:20,680 --> 00:27:22,680
I'm the one who should apologize.

352
00:27:24,120 --> 00:27:25,920
I understood too late.

353
00:27:27,720 --> 00:27:30,560
I thought not mentioning my brother
would make you happy.

354
00:27:34,520 --> 00:27:35,920
But I failed to consider

355
00:27:36,680 --> 00:27:39,280
that if Guanqi ever came back to see us

356
00:27:39,360 --> 00:27:41,160
and we had forgotten him,

357
00:27:42,520 --> 00:27:44,040
he would be so upset.

358
00:27:51,320 --> 00:27:52,760
You're right.

359
00:27:56,960 --> 00:27:58,200
Yanzhou,

360
00:27:59,120 --> 00:28:00,440
if

361
00:28:01,280 --> 00:28:02,920
you ever miss your brother,

362
00:28:04,040 --> 00:28:05,440
you must tell me.

363
00:28:06,280 --> 00:28:07,720
You must say so.

364
00:28:08,320 --> 00:28:09,600
All right?

365
00:28:10,680 --> 00:28:11,520
Okay.

366
00:28:12,640 --> 00:28:15,280
Then we will visit him as a family.

367
00:28:16,920 --> 00:28:18,720
How do you want to remember him?

368
00:28:18,800 --> 00:28:21,240
The things related to him,
what you remember,

369
00:28:21,320 --> 00:28:24,360
the things you know or don't know,

370
00:28:25,840 --> 00:28:27,200
I can tell you everything.

371
00:28:28,920 --> 00:28:30,000
Okay.

372
00:28:44,920 --> 00:28:49,200
<i>Yanzhou, the university learned about</i>
<i>the disinfection incident</i>

373
00:28:49,280 --> 00:28:51,200
<i>and decided to take back the key.</i>

374
00:28:51,280 --> 00:28:53,760
<i>Actually, even without this incident,</i>

375
00:28:53,840 --> 00:28:56,920
<i>this building was set</i>
<i>to be renovated this summer.</i>

376
00:28:57,600 --> 00:29:00,840
<i>After all, renovation is</i>
<i>easier than reconstruction.</i>

377
00:29:00,920 --> 00:29:03,800
<i>Unfortunately, the university</i>
<i>kept dragging its feet until now.</i>

378
00:29:03,880 --> 00:29:07,080
<i>But now, it's time to take the plunge.</i>

379
00:29:35,920 --> 00:29:37,600
Where are the things you packed?

380
00:29:39,760 --> 00:29:41,880
I seem to recall I invited you
to have dinner with me,

381
00:29:41,960 --> 00:29:43,280
not to hire you to move things.

382
00:29:44,080 --> 00:29:44,920
No charge.

383
00:29:46,840 --> 00:29:49,680
I ran into the cleaning lady
and gave everything to her.

384
00:29:49,760 --> 00:29:51,120
I'm only taking some books.

385
00:29:52,600 --> 00:29:53,720
Then let's go.

386
00:29:56,040 --> 00:29:58,840
Isn't your backpack heavy
with all those books?

387
00:30:00,800 --> 00:30:02,320
I've even carried you home.

388
00:30:03,480 --> 00:30:05,920
All right, enough about that.

389
00:30:08,520 --> 00:30:10,960
Have you noticed
you talk more than before now?

390
00:30:13,280 --> 00:30:14,640
Then I'm not talking anymore.

391
00:30:15,320 --> 00:30:18,360
Keep talking or you might burst.

392
00:30:20,240 --> 00:30:22,600
Dad, Mom, we're back.

393
00:30:26,280 --> 00:30:27,360
Hello, sir, ma'am.

394
00:30:27,440 --> 00:30:28,800
Welcome.

395
00:30:30,960 --> 00:30:32,800
The food will take a while.

396
00:30:32,880 --> 00:30:34,920
- There's some fruit there. Try some.
- Okay.

397
00:30:49,000 --> 00:30:49,840
Try some.

398
00:31:18,080 --> 00:31:19,440
Gao Xing left that.

399
00:31:20,160 --> 00:31:23,360
She said no when I offered
to bring it to her. I don't know why.

400
00:31:24,320 --> 00:31:26,560
Kids her age
don't like to wear their school uniforms.

401
00:31:49,080 --> 00:31:50,480
Stop following me.

402
00:31:54,000 --> 00:31:55,280
This seems to be my house.

403
00:31:56,440 --> 00:31:59,240
Exactly, it's your house.
Your parents are here.

404
00:32:05,680 --> 00:32:06,840
Let's eat.

405
00:32:08,800 --> 00:32:09,760
Come.

406
00:33:03,560 --> 00:33:04,960
<i>Chen Yanzhou,</i>

407
00:33:06,200 --> 00:33:08,160
<i>I once saw a film</i>

408
00:33:08,880 --> 00:33:10,400
<i>that said</i>

409
00:33:11,040 --> 00:33:13,160
<i>death isn't the end of life.</i>

410
00:33:14,000 --> 00:33:16,640
<i>As long as we are</i>
<i>still telling a person's story,</i>

411
00:33:16,720 --> 00:33:18,520
<i>they will not bow out.</i>

412
00:33:20,800 --> 00:33:23,440
<i>No solemn commemoration needed.</i>

413
00:33:23,520 --> 00:33:25,840
<i>No monumental reconciliation needed.</i>

414
00:33:27,480 --> 00:33:30,280
<i>Just when you least expect it,</i>

415
00:33:30,360 --> 00:33:32,680
<i>their name slips out.</i>

416
00:33:33,800 --> 00:33:35,840
<i>That is a reunion.</i>

417
00:33:58,240 --> 00:34:00,600
Your house has a lot more photos now.

418
00:34:02,600 --> 00:34:03,680
My mom compiled a lot.

419
00:34:04,920 --> 00:34:06,400
You're quite observant.

420
00:34:07,160 --> 00:34:08,719
It's getting familiar.

421
00:34:08,800 --> 00:34:11,199
This is my third time coming
to your house.

422
00:34:14,199 --> 00:34:16,760
Why did you laugh? Did I remember wrong?

423
00:34:18,760 --> 00:34:20,000
Come often.

424
00:34:25,120 --> 00:34:26,080
I forgot to ask.

425
00:34:27,440 --> 00:34:30,199
That night, you were waiting here.

426
00:34:30,280 --> 00:34:32,040
Was it to give papers to Gao Xing,

427
00:34:32,120 --> 00:34:33,800
or to wish me a happy birthday?

428
00:34:34,480 --> 00:34:36,800
That day, you were in an awful mood.

429
00:34:36,880 --> 00:34:38,800
My well-wishes seemed useless.

430
00:34:40,000 --> 00:34:41,440
That means

431
00:34:41,520 --> 00:34:44,080
you waited here
just to wish me a happy birthday?

432
00:34:50,920 --> 00:34:52,679
It wasn't that they were useless.

433
00:34:53,920 --> 00:34:56,159
In fact, it wasn't my birthday.

434
00:34:57,040 --> 00:34:58,640
Then when is your birthday?

435
00:35:00,760 --> 00:35:01,600
It's a secret.

436
00:35:02,840 --> 00:35:03,680
Just wait.

437
00:35:03,760 --> 00:35:08,360
The next time my birthday comes around,
I expect your well-wishes with interest.

438
00:35:10,040 --> 00:35:11,640
I'll pay up now.

439
00:35:11,720 --> 00:35:13,720
I can't afford the compound interest.

440
00:35:15,520 --> 00:35:16,360
Now?

441
00:35:24,320 --> 00:35:25,200
Are you sure?

442
00:35:26,440 --> 00:35:27,280
I…

443
00:35:29,480 --> 00:35:30,640
I…

444
00:35:30,720 --> 00:35:32,000
Maybe next time, then.

445
00:36:01,400 --> 00:36:02,680
Did you win the lottery?

446
00:36:03,880 --> 00:36:04,760
No.

447
00:36:05,680 --> 00:36:08,480
Then why are you smiling?
Tell me. Share the joy.

448
00:36:08,560 --> 00:36:09,560
I said I didn't.

449
00:36:09,640 --> 00:36:10,680
Walk faster.

450
00:36:10,760 --> 00:36:12,080
Zheng Yu is waiting.

451
00:36:12,160 --> 00:36:13,360
Chen Yanzhou.

452
00:36:15,920 --> 00:36:19,120
We used to be in the same year.
We had an elective course together.

453
00:36:19,200 --> 00:36:22,080
Then you went on leave, and we lost touch.

454
00:36:24,680 --> 00:36:26,120
Sorry, I don't remember.

455
00:36:27,720 --> 00:36:28,960
That's okay.

456
00:36:29,040 --> 00:36:30,680
Well…

457
00:36:35,920 --> 00:36:37,160
I'll let you two talk.

458
00:36:37,880 --> 00:36:38,840
I'll wait up ahead.

459
00:36:41,560 --> 00:36:44,480
Our college had
our thesis defense today. I passed.

460
00:36:45,320 --> 00:36:47,640
So I'm afraid I won't get another chance

461
00:36:47,720 --> 00:36:49,040
to say what I want to say.

462
00:36:54,200 --> 00:36:56,280
Chen Yanzhou, do you

463
00:36:56,920 --> 00:36:57,800
have a girlfriend?

464
00:37:01,680 --> 00:37:03,040
There's someone I like.

465
00:37:04,640 --> 00:37:07,320
Have a happy graduation. Bye.

466
00:37:11,800 --> 00:37:13,160
Done eavesdropping?

467
00:37:13,760 --> 00:37:14,760
My neck has a kink.

468
00:37:15,360 --> 00:37:16,520
- Let's go.
- Eavesdropping?

469
00:37:16,600 --> 00:37:18,280
Am I that kind of person?

470
00:37:19,760 --> 00:37:22,320
"Have a happy graduation. Bye."

471
00:37:23,760 --> 00:37:25,440
You weren't there.

472
00:37:25,520 --> 00:37:27,200
It was swift and decisive.

473
00:37:27,800 --> 00:37:29,920
Isn't it nice to be liked?

474
00:37:32,320 --> 00:37:33,960
It might be a blessing to others,

475
00:37:34,040 --> 00:37:36,280
but to him, it's like a death sentence.

476
00:37:38,640 --> 00:37:39,880
What do you mean?

477
00:37:41,320 --> 00:37:43,600
He told her that there's someone he likes.

478
00:37:45,600 --> 00:37:47,200
The three of us

479
00:37:47,280 --> 00:37:49,200
are in the lab together every day.

480
00:37:50,120 --> 00:37:51,920
Where did this crush come from?

481
00:37:52,000 --> 00:37:54,840
That's why I think…

482
00:38:04,080 --> 00:38:05,680
It's an excuse to turn her down.

483
00:38:08,160 --> 00:38:09,400
Says who?

484
00:38:10,480 --> 00:38:11,960
Refuting me?

485
00:38:12,040 --> 00:38:13,520
Do you really have a crush?

486
00:38:19,480 --> 00:38:20,360
Yes.

487
00:38:20,960 --> 00:38:22,160
And…

488
00:38:23,640 --> 00:38:25,040
I really like her.

489
00:38:38,680 --> 00:38:39,800
Cheesy.

490
00:38:41,680 --> 00:38:42,840
So cheesy.

491
00:38:44,000 --> 00:38:46,800
Why are you pretending
in front of the two of us?

492
00:38:48,800 --> 00:38:50,240
No, wait a second.

493
00:38:51,600 --> 00:38:53,720
At the boss's birthday party,

494
00:38:54,880 --> 00:38:56,400
you folded your finger.

495
00:38:57,480 --> 00:38:59,120
Are you really dating?

496
00:39:00,040 --> 00:39:01,120
Who did you kiss?

497
00:39:01,200 --> 00:39:03,200
Is she from our university? Which college?

498
00:39:04,000 --> 00:39:05,160
Bi Dezheng,

499
00:39:05,240 --> 00:39:08,280
didn't you have something to say?

500
00:39:08,880 --> 00:39:10,520
What's more important than this?

501
00:39:16,200 --> 00:39:17,280
Yes.

502
00:39:17,800 --> 00:39:18,960
Let's get down to business.

503
00:39:22,160 --> 00:39:23,520
You two are such killjoys.

504
00:39:23,600 --> 00:39:25,320
Fine.

505
00:39:25,400 --> 00:39:27,120
I wanted to ask when you are free.

506
00:39:27,720 --> 00:39:30,440
We can go to a public beach
to get a seawater sample.

507
00:39:30,520 --> 00:39:32,840
Chen Yanzhou can drive, right?

508
00:39:32,920 --> 00:39:34,880
Zheng Yu and I can get a lift.

509
00:39:35,560 --> 00:39:37,800
But I haven't decided which beach.

510
00:39:38,960 --> 00:39:41,880
How about Qingshan Island?

511
00:39:41,960 --> 00:39:44,200
Fine by me. What about you?

512
00:39:45,200 --> 00:39:46,040
No problem.

513
00:39:46,880 --> 00:39:49,880
But I have to arrange leave
with the student I tutor.

514
00:39:55,920 --> 00:39:57,240
Jiang Mian.

515
00:39:57,880 --> 00:40:00,440
What took you so long?
I've been waiting a while.

516
00:40:00,520 --> 00:40:01,720
For me?

517
00:40:02,640 --> 00:40:05,160
Here's your uniform.
So you have something to wear.

518
00:40:05,240 --> 00:40:06,280
I've washed it.

519
00:40:06,360 --> 00:40:07,520
I thought you forgot.

520
00:40:07,600 --> 00:40:09,400
What do you take me for?

521
00:40:09,480 --> 00:40:10,600
Leaving already?

522
00:40:12,200 --> 00:40:13,280
MS. ZHENG

523
00:40:13,920 --> 00:40:15,160
Hi, Ms. Zheng.

524
00:40:20,800 --> 00:40:22,160
You need time off?

525
00:40:22,960 --> 00:40:24,800
Reschedule the weekend session?

526
00:40:25,400 --> 00:40:26,600
But

527
00:40:26,680 --> 00:40:29,200
final exams are coming up.

528
00:40:29,280 --> 00:40:30,960
You're putting me in a tight spot.

529
00:40:31,560 --> 00:40:34,320
What's more important than tutoring me?

530
00:40:35,600 --> 00:40:36,800
Lab stuff?

531
00:40:37,880 --> 00:40:39,840
Can't you just push through?

532
00:40:40,720 --> 00:40:41,800
<i>All right.</i>

533
00:40:41,880 --> 00:40:43,680
<i>I'll find another way.</i>

534
00:40:44,520 --> 00:40:46,240
What? You can't push through?

535
00:40:46,320 --> 00:40:48,600
Ms. Zheng, this attitude of yours…

536
00:40:48,680 --> 00:40:49,640
AGREE TO IT

537
00:40:50,880 --> 00:40:54,480
<i>Gao Xing, what are you talking about?</i>

538
00:40:54,560 --> 00:40:57,320
<i>Didn't I just say I'd find another way?</i>

539
00:40:57,400 --> 00:41:00,160
<i>Getting samples isn't hard.</i>
<i>I can ask my other teammates to go.</i>

540
00:41:00,240 --> 00:41:01,240
I'LL TUTOR YOU

541
00:41:05,120 --> 00:41:06,920
Ms. Zheng, I just remembered

542
00:41:07,000 --> 00:41:08,760
I also have plans this weekend.

543
00:41:08,840 --> 00:41:11,640
You can tutor me when you get back.

544
00:41:11,720 --> 00:41:12,560
Bye.

545
00:41:13,680 --> 00:41:15,280
You had better keep your word.

546
00:41:15,360 --> 00:41:16,880
Of course.

547
00:41:16,960 --> 00:41:19,400
I'm free both days of the weekend.
What about you?

548
00:41:33,440 --> 00:41:34,680
Get in.

549
00:41:47,840 --> 00:41:49,440
Do you know where Bi Dezheng is?

550
00:41:52,520 --> 00:41:53,440
BI DEZHENG

551
00:41:53,520 --> 00:41:54,600
ANSWER

552
00:41:55,760 --> 00:41:56,840
Where are you?

553
00:41:56,920 --> 00:41:58,480
<i>My advisor suddenly told me</i>

554
00:41:58,560 --> 00:41:59,960
<i>to go to his office.</i>

555
00:42:01,000 --> 00:42:02,880
So

556
00:42:02,960 --> 00:42:03,840
you're not coming.

557
00:42:03,920 --> 00:42:05,680
<i>Yes, I can't come.</i>

558
00:42:11,400 --> 00:42:14,080
It's such a shame
that we can't go as a team.

559
00:42:14,680 --> 00:42:16,360
<i>I can't talk. You guys go ahead.</i>

560
00:42:17,280 --> 00:42:18,440
Bye then.

561
00:42:25,760 --> 00:42:27,120
He flaked on us.

562
00:42:27,200 --> 00:42:28,720
Why do you look kind of happy?

563
00:42:30,160 --> 00:42:31,400
Do I?

564
00:42:32,760 --> 00:42:34,840
I just think

565
00:42:34,920 --> 00:42:36,720
the weather is great today.

566
00:42:45,480 --> 00:42:47,240
Are we setting out yet?

567
00:42:49,120 --> 00:42:50,560
Are you sitting there?

568
00:42:51,360 --> 00:42:52,480
What's wrong?
